[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Football or Polo?]
[00:13.84]What happened to the man in the boat?
[00:19.58]The Wayle is a small river that cuts across the park near my home.
[00:26.94]I like sitting by the Wayle on fine afternoons.
[00:31.85]It was warm last Sunday, so I went and sat on the river bank as usual.
[00:38.73]Some children were playing games on the bank and there were some people rowing on the river.
[00:46.51]Suddenly, one of the children kicked a ball very hard and it went towards a passing boat.
[00:55.47]Some people on the bank called out to the man in the boat, but he did not hear them.
[01:02.83]The ball struck him so hard that he nearly fell into the water.
[01:09.01]I turned to look at the children, but there weren't any in sight: they had all run away!
[01:16.94]The man laughed when he realized what had happened.
[01:20.91]He called out to the children and threw the ball back to the bank.
